# Cards added to the tailnet index (tailscale.harm.org) for the observability
# surfaces: Grafana, Prometheus, Alertmanager. The index lives at
# ~/git/tailscale-index/site/index.html (served by server.py on 127.0.0.1:3912,
# fronted by cloudflared as tailscale.harm.org). That dir is NOT a git repo, so
# this is a provenance record of the applied edit, not an auto-applied patch.
# These three targets bind the tailnet IP directly (not tailscale-serve), so
# their links were http:// (tailnet), unlike the https:// serve URLs on the other
# cards. Applied 2026-07-21.
#
# UPDATE 2026-07-22: *.ts.net is HSTS-preloaded, so browsers force HTTPS on the
# tailnet hostname and a bare http://…:port target is unreachable (TLS handshake
# to a plain-http port fails) — that is why the Grafana card read as "broken".
# Fixed Grafana by fronting it with tailscale-serve TLS:
#   sudo tailscale serve --bg --https=8853 http://100.85.100.81:3003
# and repointing the card to https://proximal.tail0ecc2e.ts.net:8853/ (+ set
# Grafana root_url to that Serve URL; see grafana-server.env.overrides). The
# Prometheus (:9091) and Alertmanager (:9093) cards still bind the tailnet IP
# directly over http and remain browser-unreachable for the same reason — front
# them the same way when they're wanted from a browser.
--- a/site/index.html
+++ b/site/index.html
@@ -212,6 +212,39 @@
         <article class="service">
           <div>
             <h2>Harm Site Mirror</h2>
             <a href="https://proximal.tail0ecc2e.ts.net:8890/">https://proximal.tail0ecc2e.ts.net:8890/</a>
           </div>
           <span class="tag">tailnet mirror</span>
         </article>
